# Terraform local state and provider cache - never committed. The lock
# file (.terraform.lock.hcl) is the opposite: always committed, per each
# root module's own directory, so the negation below is explicit rather
# than relying on it simply not matching a broader "**/.terraform/" glob.
**/.terraform/
**/terraform.tfstate
**/terraform.tfstate.*
**/*.tfplan
**/crash.log
**/crash.*.log
!**/.terraform.lock.hcl

# Real variable values - only *.tfvars.example is committed.
**/*.tfvars
!**/*.tfvars.example

# Generated by `terraform output -json > outputs.json` (see bootstrap/README.md)
# - holds a real lab's public IPs, never committed.
bootstrap/outputs.json

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
